---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Draft privacy policy for ServiceNow Learn Easy."
  updated="14 November 2026"
>
  <p>
    This draft describes the data the planned learning platform expects to collect. It must be
    reviewed and completed before any real student data is collected.
  </p>

  <h2>Information we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Account details: name, email address, profile image if you use Google sign-in, and role.
    </li>
    <li>Learning data: course enrollments, lesson completion, and last playback position.</li>
    <li>Order data: course, amount, currency, payment status, and payment provider order ID.</li>
    <li>
      Technical data: error logs and basic request data needed to operate and secure the service.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How we use information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To create and secure your account.</li>
    <li>To verify payment and grant course access.</li>
    <li>To save progress and show it on another device.</li>
    <li>To answer support requests and investigate abuse.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Payment processing</h2>
  <p>
    Payment is planned through Razorpay. Card and bank details are entered in the payment provider's
    interface. This platform does not store full card numbers or payment credentials. It stores
    order IDs, amounts, and payment status.
  </p>

  <h2>Service providers</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Firebase Authentication for sign-in and account tokens.</li>
    <li>Cloud Firestore for profile, enrollment, order, and progress records.</li>
    <li>Cloudflare Pages and Functions for hosting and server-side requests.</li>
    <li>Razorpay for payment processing and webhook notifications.</li>
    <li>YouTube for video playback. YouTube may set its own cookies and collect playback data.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Cookies and local storage</h2>
  <p>
    The planned site uses browser storage for sign-in state and interface preferences. It does not
    use advertising cookies. The final cookie list must be confirmed after the authentication and
    video integrations are complete.
  </p>

  <h2>Retention</h2>
  <p>
    Account, enrollment, and order records are kept while the account is active and for the period
    required for tax, accounting, and dispute handling. Progress records are kept while the
    enrollment is active. Final retention periods require legal review.
  </p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    Access tokens are verified on the server. Payment events are verified by signature. Firestore
    rules deny client writes to commercial and access-control records. No system is completely
    secure, and the platform does not claim otherwise.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>
    You may request access, correction, or deletion of your account data. Some records may be
    retained where the law requires it. A working request channel will be published before launch.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    The service is intended for working professionals. It is not directed to children. The minimum
    age and parental-consent process require legal review.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    This draft will change. A revised version will be published with a new date before production
    use.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Contact details are placeholders in this preview. Use the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>{' '}
    for the current review channel.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
